# Known, accepted divergences between the record and the repository.
#
# This is a baseline, not a silencer. Every key listed here is still printed in
# full by check_record_drift.py on every run, with the record's own words and
# the contradicting fact — listing it only stops it failing the build. The point
# is that NEW drift still fails, which is the whole value of the check.
#
# Each line needs a reason after '#'. An entry without one is a configuration
# error and fails, deliberately: an unexplained exemption is worse than none.
#
# Every entry below is filed as an issue and awaits a ruling on the canonical
# record, which is the operator's to make and not something CI should be able to
# force. Delete a line when its issue closes — the check failing again at that
# point is it confirming the fix landed.

A/experiments/gpt2_small/spectral_resonance.ipynb  # issue #54 — H4's scaffold carries executed output reading NOT SUPPORTED (mean |cos| 0.2387, 5/144 heads > 0.9) while FINDINGS, JOURNEY_MAP and README still call it not run. Whether an artifact-recovery run under ATR_PAUSE disposes of a pre-registered hypothesis is the operator's ruling.

D/experiments/gpt2_small/spectral_resonance.ipynb  # issue #54 — the same notebook's own "Not yet run" banner sits above those executed cells. Fixing the banner is safe, but it should say the same thing the disposition ends up saying, so it waits on the same ruling.

